287
00:24:18,390 --> 00:24:21,020
Please!

288
00:24:21,020 --> 00:24:23,240
Yes yes yes yes!

289
00:24:26,550 --> 00:24:29,040
Oh no oh no...

290
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:39,040
Yes!

291
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:47,340
Oh, here we go! It's beans!

292
00:24:47,130 --> 00:24:49,630
Mm.

293
00:24:49,630 --> 00:24:52,530
Okay.

294
00:24:52,530 --> 00:24:56,270
Beans, huh.

295
00:24:56,270 --> 00:24:59,310
Hey.

296
00:24:59,310 --> 00:25:02,210
Ugh, beans...

297
00:25:02,210 --> 00:25:06,510
There's no way I can clear this with a time limit, this is insane.

298
00:25:06,510 --> 00:25:10,460
Just one?

299
00:25:17,870 --> 00:25:21,240
There's a time limit?! Why, why, why!

300
00:25:24,870 --> 00:25:31,870
Wait, isn't this impossible?!

301
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:38,090
Here—

302
00:25:38,290 --> 00:25:43,670
And I can't even roll it anywhere!

303
00:25:43,670 --> 00:25:48,570
Oh, there's a raised edge — clever design.

304
00:25:48,570 --> 00:25:54,170
So the same trick as before won't work, huh.

305
00:25:54,170 --> 00:25:58,730
But there's no height difference here either.

306
00:25:58,730 --> 00:26:01,300
See—

307
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:08,440
Oh, I think I can grab it!

308
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:12,190
Good work.

309
00:26:54,700 --> 00:27:00,220
There's no way anyone can clear that within the time limit.

310
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:05,380
Hm?

311
00:29:11,650 --> 00:29:12,850
Hold on a sec.

312
00:29:12,850 --> 00:29:18,830
If there are more beans—

313
00:29:18,830 --> 00:29:20,170
I might be able to grab one.

314
00:29:20,170 --> 00:29:23,450
On the side—

315
00:29:23,450 --> 00:29:30,060
31 seconds.

316
00:29:30,060 --> 00:29:33,050
And also—

317
00:29:33,050 --> 00:29:34,850
Going by how things have been so far—

318
00:29:34,850 --> 00:29:35,850
I mean, how things have been—

319
00:29:35,850 --> 00:29:38,510
I've only done the tofu stage so far, but—

320
00:29:38,510 --> 00:29:41,570
Going by the pattern so far—

321
00:29:41,570 --> 00:29:42,810
Next one's gonna be beans again, isn't it.

322
00:29:42,810 --> 00:29:45,350
Round 2.

323
00:29:54,420 --> 00:29:58,020
This makes no sense.

324
00:30:45,150 --> 00:30:47,150
Hmm.

325
00:30:49,150 --> 00:30:50,630
Hmm.

326
00:30:54,550 --> 00:30:58,710
Wait, what?

327
00:30:58,710 --> 00:31:06,150


328
00:31:14,210 --> 00:31:18,210
Oh, so close! I almost had it that time, I swear!

329
00:31:45,500 --> 00:31:48,210
Okay, okay, hold on.

330
00:32:01,210 --> 00:32:03,210
Wait, no no no.

331
00:32:11,210 --> 00:32:12,210
Huh, wait—

332
00:32:12,210 --> 00:32:14,210
Hold on, hold on!

333
00:32:16,470 --> 00:32:18,470
What?! The bean just balanced on it!

334
00:32:20,550 --> 00:32:21,550
The bean is on there!

335
00:32:22,350 --> 00:32:23,350
Is that allowed?!

336
00:32:30,810 --> 00:32:32,810
Yes!!

337
00:32:37,890 --> 00:32:39,470
The narration in this game

338
00:32:39,270 --> 00:32:41,410
is based on the book by Edward Wang

339
00:32:41,410 --> 00:32:43,230
