340
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:47,670
As the book also states,

341
00:32:47,670 --> 00:32:50,850
the first use of chopsticks in human history

342
00:32:50,850 --> 00:32:53,310
is believed to have been in ancient China.

343
00:32:53,110 --> 00:32:54,110
Mm-hmm.

344
00:32:54,960 --> 00:33:00,110
Okay.

345
00:33:01,770 --> 00:33:02,110
Mm-hmm.

346
00:33:03,220 --> 00:33:12,110
Okay.

347
00:33:13,230 --> 00:33:14,110
Mm-hmm.

348
00:33:16,910 --> 00:33:18,310
What's this?

349
00:33:18,310 --> 00:33:18,610
What is this?

350
00:33:18,410 --> 00:33:19,610
What is this thing?

351
00:33:21,110 --> 00:33:31,110
Wha— it disappeared!

352
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:36,320
This is so hard!

353
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:38,850
It's a dark scene.

354
00:33:55,940 --> 00:33:59,260
Well, if that's what you want, fine, I guess.

355
00:33:59,060 --> 00:34:00,640
Huh?! There's a time limit?!

356
00:34:23,410 --> 00:34:25,210
No way.

357
00:34:25,010 --> 00:34:35,010
Are you kidding me?! Did you really not notice the time limit?!

358
00:34:52,210 --> 00:34:56,600
This is brutal for someone who's been cheating this whole time!

359
00:35:17,030 --> 00:35:20,290
Just stab it! Stab it!

360
00:35:22,210 --> 00:35:28,450


361
00:35:32,110 --> 00:35:35,970
Amazing — this bowl actually spins, you know.

362
00:35:36,010 --> 00:35:42,100
It keeps sticking to the chopstick, it keeps sticking!

363
00:35:42,100 --> 00:35:44,840
It's sticking to the front chopstick!

364
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:49,500
Why does it start moving when I put one piece on?

365
00:35:49,500 --> 00:35:50,700
Battery?

366
00:35:50,700 --> 00:35:59,550
It's just a sub-objective anyway, so it's fine, right?

367
00:36:03,680 --> 00:36:09,930
Even without the time limit.

368
00:36:10,510 --> 00:36:11,290
It's so dark.

369
00:36:11,290 --> 00:36:13,970
It's too dark.

370
00:36:13,970 --> 00:36:18,620
This is not something you do in the dark.

371
00:36:18,620 --> 00:36:23,820
It's sticking.

372
00:36:23,820 --> 00:36:32,560
It's stuck.

373
00:36:32,560 --> 00:36:37,910
I can't even hold it anymore.

374
00:36:42,630 --> 00:36:49,550
lol the 3-second rule is gone

375
00:36:49,550 --> 00:36:51,230
Right?

376
00:36:51,230 --> 00:36:55,320
Something got stabbed.

377
00:36:55,320 --> 00:36:58,160
Roll it.

378
00:36:58,160 --> 00:36:59,960
Roll it!

379
00:37:02,450 --> 00:37:04,250
If I roll it, it resets.

380
00:37:04,250 --> 00:37:06,250
So I roll it.

381
00:37:07,650 --> 00:37:09,650
Roll the rice!

382
00:37:21,450 --> 00:37:23,450
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

383
00:37:24,250 --> 00:37:26,250
Nice!

384
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:48,080
What is going on here?

385
00:37:57,920 --> 00:37:59,840
Anyone watching this would get so mad.

386
00:38:00,780 --> 00:38:05,360
Like, if someone who actually cooks saw this—

387
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:10,260
It keeps sticking to the chopstick — is it because it's rice?

388
00:38:10,260 --> 00:38:12,880
Ugh, come on!

389
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:16,680
Well, rice is sticky by nature.

390
00:38:16,680 --> 00:38:20,580
They say rice turns into glue, right?

391
00:38:20,580 --> 00:38:25,190
So of course it sticks to chopsticks too.

392
00:38:25,190 --> 00:38:27,120
Ugh.

393
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:33,560
Come on, come on, come on!

394
00:38:38,490 --> 00:38:46,170
Yes! Look how much I've improved!

395
00:38:47,590 --> 00:38:49,590
Let's go!

396
00:38:55,990 --> 00:38:58,990
Whoa! Gyoza! It's gyoza!

397
00:39:01,570 --> 00:39:05,350
So what do I do — carry the gyoza to the bowl?

398
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:09,560
Hold on, this thing is in the way—

399
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:11,560
Let me just—

400
00:39:20,050 --> 00:39:21,590
It won't move.

401
00:39:25,210 --> 00:39:26,770
This thing is in the way.

402
00:39:26,570 --> 00:39:28,570
Okay.

403
00:39:49,470 --> 00:39:50,470
Toss it!

404
00:40:03,040 --> 00:40:04,040
Alright.

405
00:40:05,180 --> 00:40:06,180
Here we go!

406
00:40:06,340 --> 00:40:08,340
Oh.

407
00:40:16,340 --> 00:40:18,340
Hm?

408
00:40:23,100 --> 00:40:25,610
Wait, wait, wait! I didn't mean to do that! What just happened?!

409
00:40:27,340 --> 00:40:29,380
Whoa!

410
00:40:29,180 --> 00:40:31,360
Carry the noodles to the bowl.

411
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:35,580
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

412
00:40:36,300 --> 00:40:38,080
It's just one noodle! One single noodle!

413
00:40:41,130 --> 00:40:42,630
Wow, this is actually pretty hard.

414
00:40:44,950 --> 00:40:46,450
This is really hard!

415
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:49,780
It got all tangled up like a coffee cup.

416
00:40:58,120 --> 00:41:00,020
Wait, how do I even...?

417
00:40:59,820 --> 00:41:01,820
Okay.

418
00:41:29,820 --> 00:41:31,420
Alright.

419
00:41:32,810 --> 00:41:38,290


420
00:41:39,510 --> 00:41:41,830
What is this? What even is this, everyone?

421
00:41:41,830 --> 00:41:43,110
Is that soup?

422
00:41:44,350 --> 00:41:46,270
Do I just need to move this one thing?

423
00:41:46,950 --> 00:41:49,970
Oh no, oh no, oh no, oh no...

424
00:41:50,170 --> 00:41:51,710
Whoa whoa whoa whoa!

425
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:59,000
Wait, does it count as being in there?

426
00:42:02,240 --> 00:42:03,520
Um...

427
00:42:03,900 --> 00:42:05,480
Hey now...

428
00:42:05,620 --> 00:42:09,410
I definitely did not do that on purpose, okay? That doesn't count.

429
00:42:09,410 --> 00:42:10,580
I didn't mean to.

430
00:42:11,850 --> 00:42:13,350
Aw, that didn't work.

431
00:42:14,630 --> 00:42:17,370
It's counting one as already in there!

432
00:42:19,810 --> 00:42:22,730
This leaf is so hard to grab!

433
00:42:24,230 --> 00:42:26,230
Seriously, this leaf is so difficult!

434
00:42:36,110 --> 00:42:38,110
What do I do?

435
00:42:41,110 --> 00:42:43,910
It's gone, it disappeared!

436
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:48,510
Can you please stop disappearing on me?

437
00:42:51,260 --> 00:42:54,110
There's no way if it just vanishes like that!

438
00:42:57,180 --> 00:42:59,180
What do I do?

439
00:43:00,220 --> 00:43:04,480
Oh, it moved again.

440
00:43:04,480 --> 00:43:08,420
Can I grab two at once?

441
00:43:08,420 --> 00:43:10,280
Guess not.

442
00:43:10,280 --> 00:43:14,250
Wait, what?

443
00:43:14,250 --> 00:43:18,800
lol I don't even need to grab it

444
00:43:18,800 --> 00:43:24,510
I don't need to grip it at all!

445
00:43:24,510 --> 00:43:28,310
Why am I even trying to move it?

446
00:43:28,310 --> 00:43:36,490
Why do I have to transfer it to that bowl?

447
00:43:36,490 --> 00:43:39,490
I wonder what dish this even is.

448
00:43:40,290 --> 00:43:44,290
Maybe it's a garnish? But it looks like an edible leaf though.

449
00:43:45,090 --> 00:43:47,090
I can't get it on there.

450
00:43:51,140 --> 00:43:54,140
The plate doesn't move.

451
00:43:56,680 --> 00:43:58,680
You're the one that has to move.

452
00:43:59,590 --> 00:44:03,190
Wait, seriously?

453
00:44:15,630 --> 00:44:17,630
Oh, got it!

454
00:44:17,630 --> 00:44:22,490
I did it properly, everyone!

455
00:44:22,490 --> 00:44:23,560
Legitimately.

456
00:44:23,560 --> 00:44:27,920
No funny business.

457
00:44:27,920 --> 00:44:30,000
Normal gameplay.

458
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,660
Wait, it's sinking, it's sinking — this is bad!

459
00:44:31,660 --> 00:44:32,960
Oh no, this is bad!

460
00:44:32,960 --> 00:44:34,620
It's soaking in there!

461
00:44:34,620 --> 00:44:37,140
Kelp salad with dressing...

462
00:44:37,140 --> 00:44:43,840
Today's special: Chef's Whim Salad.

463
00:44:43,840 --> 00:44:46,340
Today we have—

464
00:44:46,340 --> 00:44:48,840
Two torn pieces of green leaf lettuce,

465
00:44:48,840 --> 00:44:50,660
and the dressing...

466
00:44:50,660 --> 00:44:51,640
